{%- if settings.cart_type == 'drawer' -%}
  <div id="CartDrawer" class="drawer drawer--right">
    <form id="CartDrawerForm" action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post" novalidate class="drawer__contents" data-location="cart-drawer">
      <div class="drawer__fixed-header">
        <div class="drawer__header appear-animation appear-delay-1">
          <div class="h2 drawer__title">{{ 'cart.general.title' | t }}</div>
          <div class="drawer__close">
            <button type="button" class="drawer__close-button js-drawer-close">
              <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" role="presentation" class="icon icon-close" viewBox="0 0 64 64"><title>icon-X</title><path d="m19 17.61 27.12 27.13m0-27.12L19 44.74"/></svg>
              <span class="icon__fallback-text">{{ 'cart.general.close_cart' | t }}</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="drawer__inner">
        <div class="drawer__scrollable">
          {% comment %}
            ORDER CHANGED 30 Aug 2026 ON OPERATOR INSTRUCTION, to follow the
            Overtone cart he supplied as the reference. THIS REVERSES THE
            28 Aug 2026 ORDERING DECISION, which put the delivery block under
            the bottles so the countdown was read after the cart contents.
            The reference puts the free-delivery progress FIRST, because it is
            the thing that changes what the customer buys, and on a phone
            anything below the fold is not read at all.
            If this is ever reversed again, record why, because it has now
            moved twice.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% render 'tl-delivery-summary' %}

          <div data-products class="appear-animation appear-delay-2"></div>

          {% comment %}
            JOINING GIFT, 30 Aug 2026. Sits with the bottles rather than in
            the footer, so it never pushes the checkout button down. It
            captures nothing itself: it opens the newsletter popup, which is
            the only capture on this site proven to work.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% render 'tl-joining-gift' %}

          {% comment %}
            Safe place field. No signature model, operator ruling 26 Jul 2026, implemented
            24 Aug 2026. COLLAPSED 28 Aug 2026 on operator instruction: presentation only.
            THE WORDING BELOW IS UNCHANGED AND IS WITH THE SOLICITOR. The bolded at-your-risk
            line is the fence against abuse: chosen safe place plus delivery record counts as
            delivered. Do not edit, shorten or reflow that sentence. The <details> element is
            open by default when the customer has already written a note, so nothing they typed
            is ever hidden from them.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% if settings.cart_notes_enable %}
            <details class="appear-animation appear-delay-3 tl-note"{% if cart.note != blank %} open{% endif %}>
              <summary class="tl-note__summary">Add delivery instructions</summary>
              <label for="CartNoteDrawer">Where should we leave it if you're out?</label>
              <p class="tl-note__help">Optional. Somewhere secure at your address, out of sight and out of the weather. <strong>Left there at your risk. Once the delivery record shows it was left in your chosen place, it counts as delivered.</strong> If nobody is in, Royal Mail may leave it with a neighbour aged 18 or over.</p>
              <textarea name="note" class="input-full cart-notes" id="CartNoteDrawer" rows="2">{{ cart.note }}</textarea>
            </details>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        <div class="drawer__footer appear-animation appear-delay-4">
          <div data-discounts>
            {% if cart.cart_level_discount_applications != blank %}
              <div class="cart__discounts cart__item-sub cart__item-row">
                <div>{{ 'cart.general.discounts' | t }}</div>
                <div class="text-right">
                  {% for cart_discount in cart.cart_level_discount_applications %}
                    <div class="cart__discount">
                      {{ cart_discount.title }} (-{{ cart_discount.total_allocated_amount | money }})
                    </div>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          <div class="cart__item-sub cart__item-row">
            <div class="ajaxcart__subtotal">{{ 'cart.general.subtotal' | t }}</div>
            <div data-subtotal>{{ cart.total_price | money }}</div>
          </div>

          {% comment %}
            28 Aug 2026. Replaced the theme default, which read shipping, taxes and discount
            codes calculated at checkout. Three faults: it said shipping where every other
            surface says delivery; it implied tax is added at checkout when prices are
            tax-inclusive; and it offered a discount code field that does not exist in this
            drawer. The cart page carries the same correction.
          {% endcomment %}
          <div class="cart__item-row text-center">
            <small>Delivery calculated at checkout.<br /></small>
          </div>

          {% comment %}
            AGE AND TERMS TICK. THE LABEL WORDING AND THE TICK ITSELF ARE UNTOUCHED, 28 Aug 2026.
            It is not known whether this tick is the due-diligence record under sections 146 to 147
            Licensing Act 2003, so nothing about what it asks or whether it blocks has been changed.
            That question is with the solicitor. WHAT DID CHANGE is only the failure message:
            theme.js answers an unticked box with a native browser alert(), which on a phone is a
            system popup at the moment of checkout. The script below replaces it with inline text.
            FAIL-SAFE BY DESIGN: it does not disable the theme's own check. If this script fails to
            load, theme.js still blocks checkout with its alert. The tick always blocks either way.
            30 Aug 2026: the LETTER-SPACING AND CAPITALS were removed in CSS so it reads on two
            lines instead of four. Presentation only. Not one word changed.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% if settings.cart_terms_conditions_enable %}
            <div class="cart__item-row cart__terms">
              <input type="checkbox" id="CartTermsDrawer" class="cart__terms-checkbox">
              <label for="CartTermsDrawer">
                {% if settings.cart_terms_conditions_page != blank %}
                  {{ 'cart.general.terms_html' | t: url: settings.cart_terms_conditions_page.url }}
                {% else %}
                  {{ 'cart.general.terms' | t }}
                {% endif %}
              </label>
              <p class="cart__terms-error" data-tl-terms-error hidden>Please tick the box above to continue.</p>
            </div>
          {% endif %}

          {% comment %}
            ONE CHECKOUT BUTTON, 30 Aug 2026, operator instruction, following the
            Overtone reference. THE EXPRESS WALLET BUTTONS ARE REMOVED FROM THIS
            DRAWER ONLY. Shop Pay, Apple Pay and PayPal all still appear at
            checkout, so no payment method is lost; the customer taps Check out
            first. They were roughly 300px of a phone screen and had squeezed the
            bottle list down to a single row.
            TO PUT THEM BACK, restore:
              {% raw %}{% if additional_checkout_buttons and settings.cart_additional_buttons %}{% endraw %}
              a div with class additional-checkout-buttons, containing
              {% raw %}{{ content_for_additional_checkout_buttons }}{% endraw %}
          {% endcomment %}
          <div class="cart__checkout-wrapper">
            <button type="submit" name="checkout" data-terms-required="{{ settings.cart_terms_conditions_enable }}" class="btn cart__checkout">
              {{ 'cart.general.checkout' | t }}
            </button>

            <button type="button" class="tl-continue js-drawer-close">Continue shopping</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {% comment %}
        Empty state, 28 Aug 2026. Was one sentence and no way out, so anyone who opened the
        bag out of curiosity had to close it by hand. Points at Cases because that is where
        the order value is. Since 17 Oct 2026 the welcome offer is not cases only: it is
        ten pounds off a first order of 110 pounds or more of wine.
      {% endcomment %}
      <div class="drawer__cart-empty appear-animation appear-delay-2">
        <div class="drawer__scrollable">
          <p>{{ 'cart.general.empty' | t }}</p>
          <div class="tl-empty__actions">
            <a href="/collections/cases" class="btn btn--full">Shop the cases</a>
            <a href="/collections/all-wines" class="text-link tl-empty__secondary">Or browse every wine</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>

  <style>
    .tl-note{margin-top:14px}
    .tl-note__summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;list-style:none;padding:4px 0}
    .tl-note__summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
    .tl-note__summary::after{content:" +";text-decoration:none}
    .tl-note[open] .tl-note__summary::after{content:" \2212"}
    .tl-note[open] .tl-note__summary{margin-bottom:6px}
    .tl-empty__actions{margin-top:18px}
    .tl-empty__secondary{display:block;margin-top:12px;font-size:13px}
    .cart__terms-error{margin:6px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#4A0D18;font-weight:600}
    .cart__terms.has-error .cart__terms-checkbox{outline:2px solid #4A0D18;outline-offset:2px}
    .tl-continue{display:block;width:100%;margin-top:12px;padding:6px 0;border:0;background:none;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
  </style>

  <script>
  (function () {
    // Capture phase on document, so this runs BEFORE the theme's own submit handler
    // and the native alert never fires. Listeners attached to the form itself would
    // run in registration order and could not be relied on to go first.
    document.addEventListener('submit', function (evt) {
      var form = evt.target;
      if (!form || !form.querySelector) return;

      var box = form.querySelector('.cart__terms-checkbox');
      var btn = form.querySelector('.cart__checkout');
      if (!box || !btn) return;
      if (btn.getAttribute('data-terms-required') !== 'true') return;
      if (box.checked) return;

      evt.preventDefault();
      evt.stopPropagation();
      btn.classList.remove('btn--loading');

      var wrap = box.closest('.cart__terms');
      var msg = form.querySelector('[data-tl-terms-error]');
      if (wrap) wrap.classList.add('has-error');
      if (msg) msg.hidden = false;
      try { box.focus({ preventScroll: false }); } catch (e) { box.focus(); }

      if (!box.dataset.tlBound) {
        box.dataset.tlBound = '1';
        box.addEventListener('change', function () {
          if (!box.checked) return;
          if (wrap) wrap.classList.remove('has-error');
          if (msg) msg.hidden = true;
        });
      }
    }, true);
  })();
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
